Conquest and multilingual England", "children": [{"id": "8567ef0d-c2c9-4fbf-ad9b-87392f3de484", "type": "concept", "title": "Norman Conquest"}, {"id": "f76e0efe-125c-4055-b70f-4feac0f0e643", "type": "concept", "title": "Anglo-Norman"}, {"id": "92e4ec6e-60a5-4bce-99ee-6f30e50a14cc", "type": "concept", "title": "trilingualism"}, {"id": "033fbc70-4dd6-48b4-bf67-238df228135f", "type": "concept", "title": "French loanword"}, {"id": "ad4afb6e-3c21-41ff-9f0e-d45a4740cb4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Latin"}, {"id": "a2924ef7-5194-4fa4-ab02-e465617f4474", "type": "concept", "title": "diglossia"}], "description": "Students learn how French, Latin, and English interacted in law, literature, church, and everyday life."}, {"id": "e7941a96-8e2f-4a0f-992b-9903d3bd917b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Middle English grammar and dialects", "children": [{"id": "b95bb4c1-d0f5-463a-87ae-9c223011b7bc", "type": "concept", "title": "inflectional leveling"}, {"id": "6354cb7d-87a0-46be-9057-3d64d0ff7eca", "type": "concept", "title": "case loss"}, {"id": "b48221a9-ac74-4bde-8b8b-0142a2b72ba1", "type": "concept", "title": "Chancery Standard"}, {"id": "fd29a09f-4fc5-499b-b370-ff3da44b786e", "type": "concept", "title": "dialect"}, {"id": "7a5cfbd2-66f9-4e62-8564-14b5d963e55a", "type": "concept", "title": "plural -s"}, {"id": "6e17a0b6-7f4a-4829-a95b-d00626097579", "type": "concept", "title": "word order"}], "description": "This subtopic examines the loss of many inflections and the rise of regional written forms."}, {"id": "852e03e6-7f66-4596-bb72-c1c397c438fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Middle English texts", "children": [{"id": "693f0fa2-ce94-4ad6-a44b-335e8bd5993c", "type": "concept", "title": "Chaucer"}, {"id": "f6922714-8d41-4633-8f3c-48b1c8892b3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Piers Plowman"}, {"id": "899bab52-7e0f-43f3-ad10-83dd85766d71", "type": "concept", "title": "Sir Gawain and the Green Knight"}, {"id": "a60395fd-5360-4d39-ba96-c4e58ba4a90c", "type": "concept", "title": "manuscript"}, {"id": "0e46b3be-f27f-4fce-9599-65bf6e89c339", "type": "concept", "title": "scribe"}, {"id": "8ef667a5-9c28-4011-80eb-2ab2c4034bb2", "type": "concept", "title": "orthographic variation"}], "description": "Students read language history through major texts and manuscript culture."}]}, {"id": "74e17287-0ff7-4ffe-b8c6-bb5f90d87baa", "type": "topic", "title": "Early Modern English", "description": "Early Modern English links Shakespeare, print, standardization, colonial expansion, dictionary-making, and major sound change.", "children": [{"id": "c6389a55-37ff-46e7-b633-2f6edf11ea16", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Great Vowel Shift and pronunciation", "children": [{"id": "f905a2d7-4713-4e05-bef6-1702b1a9cd70", "type": "concept", "title": "Great Vowel Shift"}, {"id": "76164963-b2de-41b7-a12c-1e77856bc75f", "type": "concept", "title": "long vowel"}, {"id": "33215b31-9b50-4a48-81d2-fe902177cfdc", "type": "concept", "title": "spelling-pronunciation gap"}, {"id": "eacfae2d-73a4-496d-acd3-cca08eff9c6d", "type": "concept", "title": "orthoepy"}, {"id": "162813df-147e-4f1a-8d36-3667095fb80f", "type": "concept", "title": "rhoticity"}, {"id": "6ae0ccba-71b0-4443-a8b2-caa422cde06f", "type": "concept", "title": "pronunciation guide"}], "description": "Students learn why English spelling and pronunciation diverged and how sound change shaped modern English."}, {"id": "569c0c1a-d0d4-4dac-882a-b215850880e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Print, standardization, and dictionaries", "children": [{"id": "3125c521-225e-49f4-81ad-6064f7bcac3c", "type": "concept", "title": "printing press"}, {"id": "3da40032-c8f9-4dd0-90e8-6453775d8a8b", "type": "concept", "title": "standardization"}, {"id": "13ac4eba-5226-470a-a0dc-4168236526a8", "type": "concept", "title": "orthography"}, {"id": "387f11ca-b9c0-4875-a198-e0570325f59c", "type": "concept", "title": "dictionary"}, {"id": "fe513ad2-62c7-49b7-a308-5f32bbe5b7f6", "type": "concept", "title": "grammar book"}, {"id": "713a9d07-c564-4b60-8da5-