retation by giving precise tools for style, voice, grammar, sound, and discourse.", "children": [{"id": "e8ae4be0-2b33-400b-ac3a-23e7833b0e9a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Linguistic stylistics", "children": [{"id": "22920c97-d6ac-43b5-906b-12bf417f6e97", "type": "concept", "title": "foregrounding"}, {"id": "05249b83-8889-484b-8400-6a1b66359544", "type": "concept", "title": "parallelism"}, {"id": "7f9c3417-c6ab-4ab5-aba9-9978f08fcb19", "type": "concept", "title": "deviation"}, {"id": "22fba77c-5569-42b9-af45-7ea42d30ab6a", "type": "concept", "title": "register"}, {"id": "d09d55c6-c77c-44af-afbe-c1e277749d1c", "type": "concept", "title": "voice"}, {"id": "2b0321ec-ad7d-4d36-8814-df7e6d4da06c", "type": "concept", "title": "discourse analysis"}], "description": "Students analyze literary style through sentence structure, sound patterning, diction, register, and discourse."}, {"id": "56b898e7-26e9-4ff5-ae42-d44f66086fbf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poetry, sound, and meter", "children": [{"id": "7ebad3c6-f36d-4ccf-a3f5-79fa13659469", "type": "concept", "title": "alliteration"}, {"id": "91b0ec61-6ef4-4f20-add3-a31b0bf96f8c", "type": "concept", "title": "assonance"}, {"id": "aea5a055-2137-4c35-9019-2d18ad911c14", "type": "concept", "title": "rhyme"}, {"id": "e1b04733-258e-4c0e-93e8-6b4118845f8c", "type": "concept", "title": "stress"}, {"id": "34bbac00-f355-4cb1-b409-10d84323e470", "type": "concept", "title": "meter"}, {"id": "a561d218-7d7d-437a-8f76-67c4f8798343", "type": "concept", "title": "prosody"}], "description": "This subtopic connects phonology and prosody to poetic effect."}, {"id": "391fd14e-3017-473e-a10f-9b1f94af8064", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Narrative voice and dialogue", "children": [{"id": "a3be719a-4214-4ec1-bb19-d5985413840f", "type": "concept", "title": "free indirect discourse"}, {"id": "7045f1d5-a96f-436c-b171-5aa86bb017e0", "type": "concept", "title": "dialect writing"}, {"id": "8ded4e22-d106-489f-bbb1-c6fb77cbcb49", "type": "concept", "title": "eye dialect"}, {"id": "2e05c2e2-36fc-4bd5-b1c7-81fe2282fe26", "type": "concept", "title": "idiolect"}, {"id": "c54da0d8-b553-4e0b-93dd-49e449596293", "type": "concept", "title": "reported speech"}, {"id": "c048c629-39fd-4686-b875-71fc9b947cfc", "type": "concept", "title": "narrator stance"}], "description": "Students use sociolinguistic tools to analyze characterization, dialect representation, and narrative authority."}]}, {"id": "25aa8544-a834-4f73-8b85-e2f182113159", "type": "topic", "title": "Etymology, OED Research, and Language History Projects", "description": "The course culminates in research that connects word history, textual evidence, language change, and cultural context.", "children": [{"id": "b6c941ed-2839-4f64-9d91-8703bb3d303d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical dictionary research", "children": [{"id": "1136c1cc-c081-47b8-96eb-0f9ecf627b6a", "type": "concept", "title": "OED entry"}, {"id": "4d52e6bf-8454-4e8e-982a-85484e607f7d", "type": "concept", "title": "etymology"}, {"id": "bcc0d6fe-f220-4b93-b1d8-17d6155c1a6e", "type": "concept", "title": "first citation"}, {"id": "dfd0a125-145d-4dae-9e5b-439e5d71efdb", "type": "concept", "title": "semantic shift"}, {"id": "733f72e6-891b-4fda-9705-24b51e52b6ea", "type": "concept", "title": "quotation evidence"}, {"id": "a626ba81-f78f-45d6-b0b8-67e34792ad77", "type": "concept", "title": "pronunciation history"}], "description": "Students learn to use the OED and related tools to trace word forms, meanings, pronunciations, and evidence."}, {"id": "14d696fd-214f-4c0c-8739-bcade43677cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Corpus and text-based projects", "children": [{"id": "b446ae4d-6671-434d-8a1b-1f1b8dc5cc27", "type": "concept", "title": "corpus query"}, {"id": "1197a4b2-aae4-41b0-89cf-139d19d1dda7", "type": "concept", "title": "concordance"}, {"id": "0a2606fe-7419-4e84-81d7-08b432a7c077", "type": "concept", "title": "collocation"}, {"id": "85b061a9-58f2-4d2b-9cd1-2e5fb228fe47", "type": "concept", "titl